# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environment (recreate with: py -3.12 -m venv venv)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/venv/
/.venv/
/env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Odoo runtime data
#   .odoo_data/ is the data_dir: filestore, sessions, compiled assets.
#   The filestore holds real attachments -- back it up separately, alongside a
#   pg_dump. It is deliberately NOT in git (binary, large, environment-local).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.odoo_data/
*.log
*.pid
.gunicorn.pid
#   logs/ and .runtime/ are created by run-odoo.ps1 / run-odoo.sh: the
#   Odoo log and the pidfile plus the start lock. The two globs above
#   already match their contents; these entries state the intent, and cover
#   anything else that lands there (a boot log, a lock directory).
/logs/
/.runtime/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local configuration
#   odoo.conf carries the database password, so it stays untracked.
#   odoo.conf.example is the tracked template -- copy it to odoo.conf and edit.
#   If you would rather version the real file (local-only repo), delete the
#   line below and run:  git add -f odoo.conf
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/odoo.conf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling
#   .claude/settings.local.json holds per-machine tool permissions. It is
#   personal configuration, not project code, so it stays untracked.
#
#   QA-3: the negation the note above promised is now here rather than pending.
#   A shared config belongs in .claude/settings.json (no .local), and with a
#   wholesale `.claude/` ignore the first person to write one would have found it
#   silently untracked -- the failure being that nothing happens, which is the
#   kind nobody notices.
#
#   Order matters and the directory rule cannot simply be negated: git will not
#   re-include a file inside an excluded *directory*, so the directory is
#   unexcluded and its contents excluded instead, leaving one file allowed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
